John McCain this summer has been running  a very humorous campaign basically  complaining that Barack Obama his  Democratic opponent is being treated  like a rock star by not just celebrities  but also by the media who worship his  every move this is ironic for several  reasons not least of which is the fact  that over the last quarter century no  Republican in national politics in  America has come close to receiving the  kind of favorable media treatment that  McCain has this is for a variety of  reasons one of which is that during the  Keating five scandal of the late 80s and  early 90s John McCain was at his sort of  political ebb he realized that he just  sits back and answers every single  question that a journalist asks suddenly  he's going to get more favorable  treatment he's used that approach ever  since except for the last few months  interestingly that's one reason another  reason is that for a long time in many  reporters who covered him in addition to  being very charmed by the access that he  gives them they're not used to hanging  out with Republicans who they find  copacetic and they're certainly not used  to hang around with military veterans  and their double triple certainly not  used to hang around with military  veterans who happen to have been  tortured in prison for five and a half  years in Vietnam so he has this sort of  magical effect and in the late 90s and  early 2000s he also was choosing one by  one issues that journalists care about  and that his own party does not if  there's anything that reporters like  besides access it's a politician going  after his own party particularly when  that party is the Republican Party and  so this has been the case with campaign  finance reform the late 90s when he was  going after Big Tobacco and even now as  he goes after you know big oil and oil  speculators he is playing to a media  base the great irony in all of this is  that this is allowed McCain to be had a  huge national profile on Tim Russert you  know more than 50 times on Jon Stewart  more than any single politician but now  that he's running against a guy who  sounds an awful lot like John McCain and  tooth  and he's beginning to realize that it's  not very fun to be on the receiving end  of it
 

